A||||7||Carrolles||Anyone have Cruise Control pictures for v-6?||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||03-19-2000||08:00 PM||||Hi,<P>I'm finally getting around to installing my JC Whitney cruise control in my 85SE v-6 4spd.<P>Can anyone please post pictures of the factory cruise control components in a v-6?  I'd like to see how the vacuum actuator and vacuum canister are mounted and how the cable is attached to the throttle body.<P>The instructions are very generic and I'd like to get it to look somewhat like original.<P>Has anyone installed one of these yet?  If so do you have pictures, suggestions?<P>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000001||wkayl||03-20-2000||03:09 PM||||I took some pictures this morning.  Check your mail.  Hope they help.||||reg||14
Z||000002||Carrolles||03-20-2000||07:07 PM||||The pictures are great.  Thanks.<P>If anyone else is interested in seeing them I can post them if Wkayl doesn't mind.<P>I'm going to look at a cheap Polaroid digital camera tonight ($59.95 at Circuit City).  If it looks good I'll get it and document the install of my JC Whitney Cruise for the Forum.<P>Thanks again,<P>Carroll||||reg||7
Z||000003||wkayl||03-20-2000||10:11 PM||||Your welcome to do as you wish with the pictures. Here is the link to the kind of camera I used to get them:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.sel.sony.com/SEL/consumer/ss5/office/digitalvideo/digital8camcorders/dcr-trv510_specs.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sel.sony.com/SEL/consumer/ss5/office/digitalvideo/digital8camcorders/dcr-trv510_specs.shtml</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||03-21-2000||07:48 AM||||I don't think you'll be happy with those cheapie digital cameras. Those are really more of a toy with the resolution of probably only 320 X 240. Try setting your monitor at that resolution to see how it looks and if you can live with it. With my camera (1.3 megapixel), I usually shoot pics at 800 X 600 resolution, but I can step up higher (1280 X 960 I think) or about 4 times better than the $50 cameras I see in Best Buy. I think you can get some of the megapixel cameras for about $300 now or about half what my parents paid for the one I have (it's about 7 months old).||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||03-21-2000||12:41 PM||||You are right.  I bought the camera last night and tried it out at home.  It has no flash or display.<P>I'm going to return it this week.<P>Oh well.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||03-21-2000||12:47 PM||||Polaroid PDC-640.  That's what I've got.  I think it runs around $180US at Wally World.  It's not the best, but it has a flash and a display.  It takes pretty good pics, too.  It's what I've been using since Christmas.||||reg||1
